  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through next Friday)\nIssued at 1140 AM CDT Sat Sep 5 2026\n\nThe main news in the extended realm concerns the heat dome shifting \ninto the Desert Southwest by mid-to-late week which opens our door \nto unsettled WNW flow along the eastern edge of the ridge. This \nchange is tied to a potent upper trough shifting from the Pacific \nNorthwest to the northern and central Great Plains by midweek, \nallowing a cold front to impact portions of the panhandles or \nbeyond come late week. Ensemble spread with this change is still \nsizable, but the potential for a pattern disruption involving \ncooler temps with rain chances may be in the offing by late week \ninto next weekend. NBM's spotty low PoPs support this signal well \nenough for now, but its toasty high temps may have room to go \nlower in later forecasts should confidence in the cold front \nimprove. Regardless, high temps look to hold well shy of record \nterritory next week.",
